A||||5||the need for speed||which would be better to use the front sway bar on the rear or an aftermarket rer bar||||1||
Z||000000||the need for speed||10-17-2000||11:16 PM||||does it matter which one you use? would they act the same or not||||reg||1
Z||000001||ratt||10-18-2000||11:57 AM||||It's cheaper to use a front bar on the rear (approx. 30 dollars total cost).  It did make a big difference in my cars' handling.  Now if it works better than an aftermarket bar I don't know.  I have only seen pictures of aftermarket bars but it looks like the arms are longer than the stock front bar.  If this is so, than I would think that a 7/8" bar with shorter arms would be a little stiffer than a 7/8" bar with longer arms (longer arm = more leverage = more twist = more sway).  The only down side with the front bar install is it takes a bit more time to install & it might be in the way if you put a trailer hitch on your car.  Well, thats my 2 cents worth.  Anybody else?||||reg||6
